{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Basic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Order.WellFounded","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Finset.Insert","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NoncommRing","lean:module:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Elem"],"declarations":100,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_neg_rule₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_neg_rule₁","kind":"theorem","line":1057,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L1057-L1072","doc":"**Negating either rule of an overlap composition negates its S-polynomial.**\n\n`spoly = lc₂ • (rule₁ · right) − lc₁ • (left · rule₂)`, and negating a rule flips\nboth its relation and its leading coefficient — so the two occurrences of the\nsign cancel in one term and reinforce in the other, giving `−spoly` either way.\n","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToZero_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToZero_neg","kind":"theorem","line":1045,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L1045-L1055","doc":"…and along negation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToZero_congr","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToZero_congr","kind":"theorem","line":1034,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L1034-L1043","doc":"Reducing to zero transfers along `CoeffEq`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.congr_source","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.congr_source","kind":"theorem","line":1019,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L1019-L1032","doc":"**The source of a chain may be replaced up to `CoeffEq`** — or the\nreplacement was already the endpoint. The disjunction is forced by `refl` being\na syntactic constructor; it is not a weakness of the proof. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.neg","kind":"theorem","line":1011,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L1011-L1017","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.neg","kind":"theorem","line":995,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L995-L1009","doc":"Negating a step negates both ends: run the same rule with `-c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.of_coeffEq_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.of_coeffEq_left","kind":"theorem","line":981,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L981-L993","doc":"A step only reads its source through `coeff`, so the source may be replaced\nby any coefficientwise-equal element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZerosFree_iff_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZerosFree_iff_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":921,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L921-L963","doc":"**`NoQuasiZerosFree` says exactly `Nonempty G` — and therefore carries no\nalgebraic content in this development** (bean qou-k6ks).\n\nThe hypothesis is threaded through `local_confluence` and its consequences to\nrecord the manuscript's standing assumption. This equivalence measures what\nthat threading actually buys, and the answer is: nothing beyond \"the\ngenerating set is non-empty\".\n\n* `←` is `noQuasiZerosFree_of_generator`: one generator gives an injective\n  context, which is all the condition asks.\n* `→` is the degenerate direction. With `G` empty every monomial is `[]`, so\n  *no* non-trivial context exists, the premise `¬(a = [] ∧ b = [])` is never\n  satisfiable, and the condition degenerates to \"every element is zero\" —\n  false for non-trivial `k`. So the property fails precisely when there is\n  no generator.\n\nThe reason it cannot do real work here is structural and worth stating:\nLeitner–Pawloski's `A` is the **quotient** `R⟨X⟩/I`, and a quasi-zero is a\nphenomenon of the quotient. This development's Gröbner–Shirshov framework\nworks entirely in the free algebra, where — as this theorem shows — the\ncondition is automatic. `Quotient.lean` now supplies `QuotAlg`, but only as a\n`Submodule` quotient; there is no ring structure on it yet, so the chapter's\n`NoQuasiZeros` cannot even be *stated* there. That, not the threading, is the\nmissing piece. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZerosFree_of_generator","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZerosFree_of_generator","kind":"theorem","line":909,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L909-L919","doc":"**The free algebra on at least one generator has no quasi-zeros.**\nLeft multiplication by a single generator is injective, which is all the\ncondition needs. (With `G` empty the free algebra is `k` itself and the\nproperty can genuinely fail — there is then no non-trivial context at all,\nso the hypothesis of `NoQuasiZerosFree` is vacuous while its conclusion is\nnot.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NoQuasiZerosFree","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NoQuasiZerosFree","kind":"def","line":901,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L901-L907","doc":"**No quasi-zeros for the free algebra `k⟨G⟩`**, with the contexts `b`, `c`\ntaken to be monomials (which span, so this is the chapter's condition) and\n\"not both `1`\" reading as \"not both the empty word\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZeros_of_neg_one_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.noQuasiZeros_of_neg_one_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":892,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L892-L899","doc":"Discharged whenever `-1 ≠ 1`: take the context `(b, c) = (1, -1)`.\n(The hypothesis is not idle — `NoQuasiZeros (ZMod 2)` is *false*, since\nevery pair `(b,c) ≠ (1,1)` in `ZMod 2` has `b·c = 0`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NoQuasiZeros","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.NoQuasiZeros","kind":"def","line":888,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L888-L890","doc":"**No quasi-zeros**, in the chapter's wording, for an abstract ring. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce_reduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce_reduces","kind":"theorem","line":860,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L860-L867","doc":"The reduction function witnesses multi-step reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce_is_normal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce_is_normal","kind":"theorem","line":851,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L851-L858","doc":"The reduction function produces normal forms. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduce","kind":"def","line":838,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L838-L849","doc":"**Reduction function**: select *the* normal form of each element.\n\nTakes `hlc` (unit leading coefficients) rather than `hgs`: what makes the\nchoice possible is existence, which is termination plus invertibility.\nWell-definedness of the *value* — that the choice does not matter — is\n`normal_form_unique`, and that is where `hgs` is genuinely needed. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:division-algorithm","label":"def:division-algorithm","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/division-algorithm.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_form_exists","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.normal_form_exists","kind":"theorem","line":805,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L805-L836","doc":"**Existence of normal forms** — the repaired statement, and a theorem.\n\nTwo differences from the axiom this replaces, and both matter:\n\n1. It carries `hlc`: every rule has a **unit leading coefficient**. Without\n   it the statement is false (see the section note).\n2. It does **not** take `hgs`. Existence of normal forms is pure termination\n   — reduce until stuck — and has nothing to do with confluence. The axiom's\n   `hgs` argument was never used by the content, and carrying it obscured\n   that the real missing hypothesis was elsewhere.\n\nProof: well-founded induction on `reduction_well_founded`. At `x`, either `x`\nis already normal (done, in zero steps), or\n`exists_singleStep_of_not_isNormalForm` produces a step `x → y`, and the\ninduction hypothesis applies at `y` precisely because `x → y`.\n\nReference: Bergman 1978, Theorem 1.2 (existence part), where the rules are\nmonic — which is what `hlc` restores. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduction_well_founded","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reduction_well_founded","kind":"axiom","line":784,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L784-L803","doc":"**Termination**: every sequence of single-step reductions is finite.\n\nEach `SingleStepReduction` strictly decreases the multiset of monomials in\nthe support under the Dershowitz–Manna ordering, which inherits\nwell-foundedness from `ord.wf`.\n\nAxiomatised because the proof requires a `Multiset (Monomial G)`\nrepresentation of `AlgElement` support, a proof that a step strictly\ndecreases it, and the Dershowitz–Manna theorem — components that need\nsubtraction and support extraction not available at this level.\n\nLives here rather than in `CompositionLemma` because it is stated purely in\nthis file's vocabulary and `normal_form_exists` below needs it.\n\nReference: Bergman 1978, §2, proof of Theorem 1.1 (termination). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isGrobnerShirshovBasis_of_single_letter_rule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isGrobnerShirshovBasis_of_single_letter_rule","kind":"theorem","line":712,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L712-L762","doc":"**The repaired predicate is satisfiable, and not only by degenerate\nsystems.**  A one-rule system whose leading monomial is a single letter is\na Gröbner–Shirshov basis: the length of the leading monomial forces every\ncomposition to have empty contexts, so every S-polynomial is\n`lc • r − lc • r`, which is zero.\n\nTogether with `one_not_reduces_to_zero` this brackets the predicate from\nboth sides — it is neither vacuously true (as it was before the repair)\nnor vacuously false. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.one_not_reduces_to_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.one_not_reduces_to_zero","kind":"theorem","line":695,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L695-L710","doc":"**`1` does not reduce to `0`.**  So `IsGrobnerShirshovBasis` is not\nsatisfied by \"everything reduces to zero\", which is exactly how the\nunrepaired definitions made it hold of every system. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm_one","kind":"theorem","line":682,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L682-L693","doc":"The unit is in normal form as soon as no rule's leading monomial is the\nempty word. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.inclusion_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.inclusion_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":669,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L669-L669","doc":"Every inclusion S-polynomial reduces to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.overlap_resolves","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.overlap_resolves","kind":"theorem","line":665,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L665-L665","doc":"Every overlap S-polynomial reduces to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis.mk","kind":"ctor","line":661,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L661-L661","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.IsGrobnerShirshovBasis","kind":"structure","line":655,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L655-L671","doc":"A rewriting system is a **Gröbner–Shirshov basis** if every\nS-polynomial (both overlap and inclusion compositions) reduces to\nthe zero element under the rewriting system.\n\nThis is the abstract formulation of the composition lemma\n(Shirshov 1962, Bokut 1976, Bergman 1978). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:groebner-basis","label":"def:groebner-basis","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/groebner-basis.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_coeff_lm_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_coeff_lm_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":647,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L647-L651","doc":"Over a commutative ring the outer leading monomial cancels outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_coeff_lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_coeff_lm","kind":"theorem","line":637,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L637-L645","doc":"The coefficient of an inclusion S-polynomial at the outer leading monomial\nis `lc(inner)·lc(outer) − lc(outer)·lc(inner)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_word_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_word_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":631,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L631-L635","doc":"Over a commutative ring the ambient word cancels outright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_coeff_word","kind":"theorem","line":615,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L615-L629","doc":"The coefficient of an overlap S-polynomial at the ambient word is\n`lc₂·lc₁ − lc₁·lc₂`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_isZero_of_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_isZero_of_self","kind":"theorem","line":595,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L595-L607","doc":"**A rule included in itself is vacuous.** Unlike the overlap case this needs\nno hypothesis on the contexts: `decomposition` says `lm = left ++ lm ++ right`,\nand lengths force both contexts empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_isZero_of_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly_isZero_of_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":576,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L576-L593","doc":"**An inclusion whose two contexts are empty is vacuous once the relations are\nproportional by the two leading coefficients.**\n\nWith `left = right = []` the S-polynomial is `lc(inner) • outer − lc(outer) •\ninner`, so it vanishes exactly when the hypothesis below holds coefficient by\ncoefficient. Both ways a shared leading monomial arises in practice satisfy it:\nthe two rules are the same rule, or they are negatives of each other with\nleading coefficients of opposite sign. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.spoly","kind":"def","line":566,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L566-L574","doc":"**The inclusion S-polynomial**, computed (no longer a free field):\n`lc(inner) • outer − lc(outer) • (left · inner · right)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.decomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.decomposition","kind":"theorem","line":564,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L564-L564","doc":"The leading monomial of the outer rule decomposes as\n`left ++ lm(inner) ++ right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.right","kind":"def","line":561,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L561-L561","doc":"Right context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.left","kind":"def","line":559,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L559-L559","doc":"Left context. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.outer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.outer","kind":"def","line":557,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L557-L557","doc":"The outer rule (whose lm contains the inner). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.inner","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.inner","kind":"def","line":555,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L555-L555","doc":"The inner rule (whose lm is contained). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":552,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L552-L552","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.InclusionComposition","kind":"structure","line":548,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L548-L564","doc":"**Inclusion composition**: when the leading monomial of one rule\nentirely contains that of another as a subword.\n\nIf `lm(g) = a ++ lm(f) ++ b`, then `S(f,g) = lc(f)·g − lc(g)·a·f·b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToNF_self_of_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.reducesToNF_self_of_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":540,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L540-L546","doc":"…so an element that is zero reduces to zero, in no steps. This is the\nGröbner–Shirshov obligation for a composition whose S-polynomial vanishes\noutright. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm_of_isZero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm_of_isZero","kind":"theorem","line":533,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L533-L538","doc":"An element that is zero is in normal form: `isNormalForm` only constrains\nmonomials with a non-zero coefficient, of which there are none. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_isZero_of_self","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly_isZero_of_self","kind":"theorem","line":513,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L513-L531","doc":"**A rule composed with itself over its whole leading monomial is vacuous.**\n\n`OverlapComposition` places no condition on `left` or `right`, so `left = right =\n[]` — the two rules leading on the *same* word — is a legal composition, and it\nis legal in particular when the two rules are the same rule. Then the two halves\nof the S-polynomial are literally the same element and it is zero.\n\nWorth having explicitly rather than as an aside: in any completeness proof the\ndegenerate shapes are as much a proof obligation as the genuine overlaps, and\nthis discharges every one of them whose two rules coincide. What it does *not*\ncover is two **distinct** rules leading on the same word — see\n`UGB.GrobnerShirshov.Hecke.DegenerateYbBs`, where that case is inhabited. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.spoly","kind":"def","line":502,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L502-L511","doc":"**The overlap S-polynomial**, computed (no longer a free field):\n`lc₂ • (rule₁ · right) − lc₁ • (left · rule₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.word","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.word","kind":"def","line":496,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L496-L500","doc":"The ambient word of an overlap composition: `left ++ overlap ++ right`,\nwhich is both `lm(rule₁) ++ right` and `left ++ lm(rule₂)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.overlap_nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.overlap_nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":494,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L494-L494","doc":"The overlap is non-empty. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.lm₂_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.lm₂_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":492,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L492-L492","doc":"The leading monomial of rule₂ decomposes as `overlap ++ right`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.lm₁_decomp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.lm₁_decomp","kind":"theorem","line":490,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L490-L490","doc":"The leading monomial of rule₁ decomposes as `left ++ overlap`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.right","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.right","kind":"def","line":488,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L488-L488","doc":"The right context (monomials after the overlap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.overlap","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.overlap","kind":"def","line":486,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L486-L486","doc":"The overlap subword. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.left","kind":"def","line":484,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L484-L484","doc":"The left context (monomials before the overlap). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.rule₂","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.rule₂","kind":"def","line":482,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L482-L482","doc":"The second rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.rule₁","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.rule₁","kind":"def","line":480,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L480-L480","doc":"The first rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":477,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L477-L477","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.OverlapComposition","kind":"structure","line":468,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L468-L494","doc":"**Overlap composition** (intersection S-polynomial):\ngiven two rules whose leading monomials overlap, the S-polynomial\nis the difference of the two ways to reduce the overlap.\n\nIf `lm(f) = a·b` and `lm(g) = b·c` with overlap `b`, then\n`S(f,g) = lc(g)·f·c − lc(f)·a·g` — for monic rules simply `f·c − a·g`.\n\nThe composition lemma states that the rewriting system is a\nGröbner–Shirshov basis iff every S-polynomial reduces to zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.eq_of_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.eq_of_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":450,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L450-L459","doc":"A normal form only reduces to itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.is_normal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.is_normal","kind":"theorem","line":448,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L448-L448","doc":"The result is in normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.reduces","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.reduces","kind":"theorem","line":446,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L446-L446","doc":"Multi-step reduction from f to nf. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF.mk","kind":"ctor","line":440,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L440-L440","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReducesToNF","kind":"structure","line":438,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L438-L448","doc":"An element `f` **reduces to normal form** `nf` if `f →* nf` and\n`nf` is in normal form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.exists_singleStep_of_not_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.exists_singleStep_of_not_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":409,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L409-L436","doc":"**The converse, with the hypothesis it actually needs**: if every rule has a\n*unit* leading coefficient, then an element not in normal form admits a step.\n\nThe hypothesis is not cosmetic bookkeeping. `isNormalForm` is a condition on\n**monomials** — no rule's leading monomial is an infix of one carrying a\nnon-zero coefficient — whereas taking a step additionally requires solving\n\n`c · lc(r) = f.coeff (a ++ lm(r) ++ b)`\n\nfor `c`. When `lc(r)` is not invertible those two conditions come apart, and\nan element can be **stuck**: reducible-looking (so not in normal form), yet\nwith no reduction available (so unable to reach one). That is not a gap in\nthis proof — it is a true statement about the reduction relation, and\n`NormalFormExistsRefutation` exhibits it concretely over `ℤ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.not_singleStep_of_isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.not_singleStep_of_isNormalForm","kind":"theorem","line":399,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L399-L407","doc":"A normal form admits no reduction step. (The converse needs every rule to\nhave an invertible leading coefficient; `isNormalForm` is the divisibility\ncondition, which is the standard one for monic rules.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.isNormalForm","kind":"def","line":387,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L387-L397","doc":"An element is in **normal form** with respect to a rewriting system\nif no leading monomial of any rule divides (appears as a subword of)\nany monomial actually occurring in the element.\n\nStated on coefficients, not on the `support` field: an element's normality\nmust not depend on the superset chosen to represent it. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:remainder-module","label":"def:remainder-module","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/remainder-module.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.cases_head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.cases_head","kind":"theorem","line":369,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L369-L385","doc":"**Head decomposition**: a run is either empty, or a first step followed by a\nrun.\n\n`MultiStepReduction` is generated at the *tail* — `step` appends a step to a\nrun — so this is the dual view, and it is the one Newman's lemma needs: the\ninduction there is on the source of the fork, so the first step has to be the\none exposed. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.trans","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L358-L367","doc":"Runs compose. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.head","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.head","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L347-L356","doc":"A single step in front of a run. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.step","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.step","kind":"ctor","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L341-L345","doc":"Transitivity: if `f →* g` and `g → h`, then `f →* h`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction.refl","kind":"ctor","line":339,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L339-L340","doc":"Zero steps: `f` reduces to itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.MultiStepReduction","kind":"inductive","line":333,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L333-L345","doc":"**Multi-step reduction**: the reflexive transitive closure of\nsingle-step reduction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.not_coeffEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.not_coeffEq","kind":"theorem","line":325,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L325-L331","doc":"In particular a step changes the element: `g ≠ f` coefficient-wise. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.exists_eliminated","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.exists_eliminated","kind":"theorem","line":309,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L309-L323","doc":"**A step eliminates the monomial it targets.**  This is what makes the\nrepaired reduction relation terminating, and it is the property the\n`reduction_well_founded` axiom of `CompositionLemma.lean` rests on. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.exists_witness","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.exists_witness","kind":"theorem","line":299,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L299-L299","doc":"There exists a rule, an occurrence of its leading monomial inside a\nmonomial of `f`, and a coefficient, witnessing the step. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction.mk","kind":"ctor","line":293,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L293-L293","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.SingleStepReduction","kind":"structure","line":272,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L272-L307","doc":"**Single-step reduction**, repaired (repair 2).\n\n`f → g` when some rule `r ∈ sys` has its leading monomial occurring inside\na monomial of `f` — say `f` has a non-zero coefficient at `a ++ lm(r) ++ b`\n— and `g` is obtained by subtracting the corresponding multiple of the\nrelation:\n\n`g = f − c • (a · r.relation · b)`,  with  `c · lc(r) = f.coeff(a·lm(r)·b)`.\n\nThe coefficient condition is what makes the step *eliminate* the monomial\nit targets: `g.coeff (a·lm(r)·b) = 0`. Two degenerate readings are excluded\nby it. Without `f.coeff (a·lm(r)·b) ≠ 0` and the equation on `c`, the\nchoice `c = 0`, `g = f` would be a legal step, `→` would be reflexive, and\n`CompositionLemma.reduction_well_founded` would be a *false* axiom. And\nthe previous version — which asked only that `lm(r)` be an infix of some\nmonomial of `f`, with no relation between `f` and `g` at all — admitted\n`g = 0` from any `f` whatsoever.\n\nEverything is stated on coefficients rather than on the `support` field,\nbecause that field is only a superset of the true support (see `Elem.lean`)\nand carries no mathematical content. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.nonempty","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.nonempty","kind":"theorem","line":270,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L270-L270","doc":"The system has at least one rule (non-trivial). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.rules","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.rules","kind":"def","line":268,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L268-L268","doc":"The collection of reduction rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem.mk","kind":"ctor","line":266,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L266-L266","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.RewritingSystem","kind":"structure","line":265,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L265-L270","doc":"A **rewriting system**: a set of reduction rules. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.lc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.lc","kind":"def","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L260-L263","doc":"The leading coefficient of a rule, for a given admissible order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.lm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.lm","kind":"def","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L255-L258","doc":"The leading monomial of a rule, for a given admissible order. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.nonzero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.nonzero","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L253-L253","doc":"The relation is non-zero. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.relation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.relation","kind":"def","line":251,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L251-L251","doc":"The polynomial whose leading term defines the rewrite. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule.mk","kind":"ctor","line":249,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L249-L249","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.ReductionRule","kind":"structure","line":245,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L245-L253","doc":"A **reduction rule**: an oriented relation `f ↦ f - c·lm(f)` that\nreplaces the leading monomial of `f` by its tail.\n\nIn practice, each defining relation of the algebra gives one rule. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingCoeff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingCoeff","kind":"def","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L238-L241","doc":"The **leading coefficient**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial_eq_of_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial_eq_of_max","kind":"theorem","line":227,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L227-L236","doc":"Pinning the leading monomial down: a support element that dominates every\nother support element *is* the leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lt_leadingMonomial_of_coeff_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.lt_leadingMonomial_of_coeff_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L215-L225","doc":"Every *other* monomial actually occurring in `f` is strictly below the\nleading monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.le_leadingMonomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.le_leadingMonomial","kind":"theorem","line":209,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L209-L213","doc":"**Maximality**: no monomial of the element exceeds the leading monomial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial_mem_support","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial_mem_support","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L203-L207","doc":"The leading monomial is a monomial of the element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.leadingMonomial","kind":"def","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L190-L201","doc":"The **leading monomial** of a non-zero element with respect to an\nadmissible order: the greatest monomial of its support.\n\n(The support may be a strict superset of the monomials with non-zero\ncoefficient — see `Elem.lean` — so the leading monomial may carry\ncoefficient `0`. `lt_leadingMonomial_of_coeff_ne_zero` is the statement\nthat survives that slack, and it is the one the theory uses.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.exists_max","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.exists_max","kind":"theorem","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L150-L181","doc":"Every non-empty finite set of monomials has a greatest element. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.not_lt_nil","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.not_lt_nil","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L131-L148","doc":"**The empty word is the minimum of any admissible order.**\n\nIf some `m` were below `[]`, right compatibility would give\n`m ++ x < x` for *every* `x`, and `x ↦ m ++ x` would be an infinite\ndescending chain — contradicting well-foundedness. Nothing in the\nstructure's fields says this directly; it is forced. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.lt_trans","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.lt_trans","kind":"theorem","line":113,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L113-L129","doc":"An admissible order is transitive.  Trichotomy alone does not give this;\nwell-foundedness does, by ruling out the 3-cycle `a < b < c < a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.irrefl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.irrefl","kind":"theorem","line":109,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L109-L111","doc":"An admissible order is irreflexive. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.asymm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.asymm","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L96-L107","doc":"An admissible order is asymmetric: well-foundedness forbids `a < b < a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.right_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.right_compat","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L89-L89","doc":"Right compatibility: `a < b → a ++ d < b ++ d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.left_compat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.left_compat","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L86-L86","doc":"Left compatibility: `a < b → c ++ a < c ++ b`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.wf","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.wf","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The order is well-founded (every non-empty set has a minimum). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.trichotomy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.trichotomy","kind":"theorem","line":81,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L81-L81","doc":"The order is a strict linear order (trichotomy). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.lt","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.lt","kind":"def","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L79-L79","doc":"The strict order relation on monomials. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder.mk","kind":"ctor","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L77-L77","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"UGB.GrobnerShirshov.AdmissibleOrder","kind":"structure","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/unital-groebner-bases/lean/UGB/GrobnerShirshov/Basic.lean#L70-L90","doc":"An **admissible monomial order**: a well-order on monomials that is\ncompatible with left and right multiplication (concatenation).\n\n`lt a b` means `a` is strictly smaller than `b` in the ordering.\n\nCompatibility: if `a < b` then `c ++ a ++ d < c ++ b ++ d`\nfor all monomials `c`, `d`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:def:admissible-system","label":"def:admissible-system","md":"unital-groebner-bases/unital-groebner-bases-chapter/admissible-system.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}